Description: KiwiSDR 37f65b4b — detect admin password == serial number (C++ backend)
 Ported from upstream commit "important security fixes/improvements"
 (37f65b4b90bb68ff81a42f8f77fe2d080bcc7809). Backend-only: adds the
 admin_pwd_unsafe() helper and the kiwi_t.serno / kiwi_t.admin_advisory
 fields it needs.
 .
 Web-888 adaptations:
  - the receiver serial number lives in net.serno (type u4_t), not
    kiwi.serno, so admin_pwd_unsafe() compares against net.serno;
  - the rev_auto / rev_auto_host / rev_host admin config keys used by the
    upstream host-comparison branch are absent on Web-888, so only the
    simplified admin_password-vs-serial comparison is retained (matching
    the upstream final logic);
  - asprintf()'d strings are freed with free(), cfg-allocated strings with
    admcfg_string_free();
  - the ui/admin.cpp call site is not wired up in this first port (the
    Web-888 admin password verification flow differs); admin_pwd_unsafe()
    is callable but currently unused, to be invoked by a future patch.
 .
 The JS pieces (admin.js, kiwi.js, openwebrx.js), cfg/cfg.cpp, the
 net/net.cpp check_if_forwarded hunk and the rx/rx_cmd.cpp serno rename
 from the upstream commit are intentionally NOT included (divergent /
 JS / absent on Web-888).
Origin: https://github.com/kiwisdr/kiwiSDR-wb66v4/ commit 37f65b4b
Forwarded: not-needed

